# CouchTato — Version Log

Newest first. Entries cover user-facing changes, notable fixes, and
anything that changes where files live or how things are configured.

Versions before 0.1.0 are reconstructed retrospectively from the change
history — they were not tagged at the time.

---

## 0.1.0

* Added adaptive text color for image backgrounds: the background image is
  sampled (downscaled to 32x32 off-screen, ~1ms, once per image load) and
  clock, weather, and the footer hint legend each get their own text color
  based on what's actually behind them. Runs per image, so slideshows
  re-evaluate on every change.
* Added high-variance detection for background regions — where a region is
  too visually busy for any single text color to work across it, that text
  gets a stronger shadow instead of a color that only half-works.
* Fixed the black/white text threshold, which was set to an
  intuitive-looking 0.4 but is mathematically 0.179 (the luminance where
  black and white give equal contrast). The old value picked white text on
  mid-gray backgrounds at 3.95:1 where black would have given 5.32:1. This
  also affected solid-color backgrounds, not just images.
* Added this version log.

## 0.0.9

* Reverted the packaging work (AppImage/.deb/.rpm builds, electron-builder,
  desktop entry) — back to running from source with `npm start`.
* Reverted `config.json` to living in the app folder. It had been moved to
  the userData folder only because a system-installed app can't write to
  its own install directory; with packaging gone, the indirection had no
  purpose.

## 0.0.8

* Added a Settings → Updates tab: current version, last-checked time, a
  "Search for update" button, and an automatic-updates toggle backed by a
  24h scheduler that survives restarts.
* Added `updater.js` as a deliberate stub — the surrounding wiring is
  complete and calls it, so filling in the real check is a one-file change.
  See DOCUMENTATION.md §3.8.

## 0.0.7

* Added a "Recently Played Songs" row to the Spotify home screen —
  individual tracks, as distinct from "Jump back in", which groups by the
  playlist/album a track was played from.
* Added playlist pinning: pinned playlists sort to the front of "Your
  Playlists" and are marked. Bound to X on the controller and the X key.
* Fixed Spotify tiles stretching to absurd heights on long playlist names —
  titles now clamp to two lines, subtitles to one, and the text panel has a
  fixed height so tiles in a row stay uniform.
* Fixed text and icons (including the settings cog and power button) going
  unreadable in Light mode with a solid-color background. The auto-contrast
  color was being applied globally, including to elements sitting on their
  own opaque panel where it never belonged. Split into two independent
  variable sets: one for panel text, one for text sitting directly on the
  background.
* Removed the track count from playlist tiles.

## 0.0.6

* Moved the Now Playing bar above the footer hint legend.
* Added a progress bar to the Now Playing bar, above the track name.
* Changed the play/pause button to reflect actual state — a pause icon when
  playing, a play icon when paused, instead of a static combined icon.

## 0.0.5

* Added accent icons to the main tiles (browser, Spotify, controller, movie
  clapperboard, folder), colored per-tile and legible in both themes.
* Added tile icon support to `config.json` via an `icon` field.
* Fixed the Kodi tile not launching — the kodi-omega snap installs its
  binary as `kodi-omega`, not `kodi`.
* Fixed `vaInitialize failed` warnings on startup in VMs. Disabling hardware
  acceleration alone didn't stop it; VAAPI decode/encode is a separate
  Chromium feature that probes independently and had to be disabled too.

## 0.0.4

* Added custom backgrounds: solid color (preset palette), single image, or
  a slideshow with configurable interval and crossfade duration.
* Added font customization — four bundled OFL-licensed families (Roboto,
  Open Sans, Merriweather, JetBrains Mono), custom font upload, plus size,
  color, and opacity. Defaults are unchanged unless explicitly set.
* Added submenu support: a tile with `"type": "submenu"` opens a nested
  grid, supporting arbitrary nesting for grouping apps.
* Fixed Light mode washing out custom backgrounds — the scrim was near-opaque
  and theme-colored; it's now a light legibility aid that leaves the
  background visible.
* Fixed long CPU names clipping in the Settings window (a flexbox
  `min-width: 0` overflow issue).
* Fixed accent colors shifting slightly between Dark and Light themes; they
  now share one definition. Light mode's text color was also darkened from a
  washed-out charcoal toward true black.

## 0.0.3

* Added a Spotify home screen with horizontally scrolling rows: search,
  Jump back in, Your Playlists, and mood/genre rows.
* Added Spotify search with an on-screen controller-navigable keyboard;
  physical keyboards can type directly.
* Added a floating overlay scrollbar for Spotify rows, replacing the
  permanent native scrollbar.
* Changed search result order to Tracks, Albums, then Playlists.

## 0.0.2

* Changed all on-screen error reporting to write to `error.log` instead —
  errors previously appeared as toasts or raw command output dumped over the
  tile grid.
* Added catch-all handlers so uncaught exceptions and rejected promises are
  logged rather than lost.
* Fixed Restart and Shutdown doing nothing from the power menu. Two stacked
  bugs: the command was spawned detached and reported success without
  waiting, and the caller never checked the result — so failures were
  invisible at both layers.

## 0.0.1

* Changed the Spotify Now Playing bar from a permanent fixture to a floating
  overlay that appears while playing and fades out after pausing.
* Replaced the local-file/VLC browsing hub with a plain Kodi launch tile —
  Kodi already provides a full library UI (posters, resume, watched state),
  so there was nothing worth rebuilding around it.
